enchilada: touch: 400 kHz I2C and the controller read when ATTN says so, looked at every 2 ms

The RMI4 path read the F01 status every 10 ms after the previous read, at 100 kHz: an 88-byte F12
report is ~820 bits, ~8.2 ms of busy wait, plus ~0.5 ms for the status. While a finger moved that is
one report per ~19 ms (~50/s) and 10-20 ms from the controller's report to the HID event; idle, 300
loops took 3.41 s (boot 5x "raw max" lines). A 50 Hz touch stream under a 60 Hz renderer moves the
content in uneven steps however fast frames are drawn.

- The SE runs at 400 kHz when sweetts=1 (mainline sdm845-oneplus-common.dtsi: i2c12 clock-frequency
  400000; GENI divider 2, high 5, low 12, cycle 24 from Linux i2c-qcom-geni's 19.2 MHz table). The
  Goodix/Focaltech path and the bq27541 bus keep 100 kHz.
- The loop looks at ATTN (gpio125, EAST tile 0x0357d000, active low) every sweetts_poll ms (default
  2) and reads the status when it is low; every 4th look reads it anyway, so a pin that never moves
  costs pace, never touch.
- "SWEET TS: last 10 s: N reports (R/s), status read on A ATTN + B blind looks; ATTN to event avg X us
  max Y us (+ up to 2 ms until looked at); raw max x= y=" while there are reports (replaces the
  "raw max" line every 300 loops).

Boot-args sweetts_khz=100 sweetts_poll=10: the old pace.

--- a/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/sweet_touch.c
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@
